  "lineage": "Urban Algiers genre codified in the 1930s-40s by El Hadj M'Hamed El Anka, who adapted Andalusi sanaa suites and malhun poetry into a mandole-led popular form — long suites opening with an instrumental istikhbar, then a slow qsida in Algerian Darija over a modal cycle, accelerating through the insiraf into fast derbouka-driven closing sections, with orchestra of mandole, banjo, qanun, violin and piano-like doubling behind a single ornamented male voice.",
